@page
@{ViewData["Title"]="Install on your existing website"; ViewData["Description"]="Configure a property, copy an isolated iframe snippet and test it on your published website. HTML, permitted WordPress blocks and Wix embeds.";}
<h1>Your existing website stays yours.</h1><ol><li>Create your property and individually named rooms or apartments. Set capacity, open dates and policies.</li><li>Record existing outside bookings and unavailable dates. Publish only when your availability is up to date.</li><li>Approve your exact website origins and choose an accent color in Install widget.</li><li>Copy the loader snippet into a page permitting scripts, or use the fixed-height iframe. Keep the hosted request-page fallback.</li><li>Test the published mobile page with a synthetic request and owner decision. Guests must save their private status links; owners must check the dashboard daily.</li></ol>
<section class="card"><h2>Which snippet?</h2><p>The recommended small JavaScript loader inserts an isolated iframe and resizes it automatically. It does not render booking controls inside your website's DOM. Direct iframe embedding is simpler when a builder restricts scripts, but needs a fixed outer height and internal scrolling. A hosted page link works when embedding is blocked.</p><p>Plain HTML uses either option. WordPress requires a permitted Custom HTML block. Wix uses supported Embed HTML or Embed a Site; nested origins and outer-container sizing must be checked. Installation is not promised on every platform or plan. Real published WordPress/Wix smoke tests remain release tasks; there is no native plugin.</p><p>Maximum ten loader containers/page, five approved exact website origins/property and responsive inner height up to 1,600px. Your site's CSP must allow the application script/frame origin. Private status opens separately and owner pages cannot be embedded.</p></section><a class="button" href="/Owner/Installation">Configure and copy your snippet</a><p><a href="/Limitations">Understand availability and notification limitations</a></p>
